  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41161608",
      "title": "Understanding & Adding Routing",
      "lectureOrder": 38,
      "videoOrder": 36,
      "sourceHash": "60b32dd18d252ba8422e787e534a0969374dbf277c21428af04cdad2656329d5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.2,
          "end": 4.38,
          "en": "So we got data fetching, and data sending,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.38,
          "end": 7.32,
          "en": "and this demo website, therefore, looks quite nice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.32,
          "end": 10.44,
          "en": "quite decent, and we learned a lot about React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.44,
          "end": 14.25,
          "en": "However, there's one last crucial feature missing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.25,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "in this website, which I'd also like to explore together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 19.923,
          "en": "with you, and that would be routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.923,
          "end": 21.453,
          "en": "Now, what's routing?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.29,
          "end": 25.98,
          "en": "Many React apps, I would say, almost all React apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.98,
          "end": 28.35,
          "en": "at least, definitely if they are anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.35,
          "end": 31.92,
          "en": "but simple demo apps, might want to have routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.92,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "which simply means that you wanna support different paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 39,
          "en": "and load different pages, different components in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39,
          "end": 40.803,
          "en": "for those different paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.88,
          "end": 45.54,
          "en": "At the moment, our demo website here, only has one path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.54,
          "end": 48.99,
          "en": "No matter if I click new post or not, the path up there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.99,
          "end": 51.423,
          "en": "the URL always stays the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.41,
          "end": 55.05,
          "en": "The disadvantage of this is that I, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.05,
          "end": 59.07,
          "en": "can't link users to this new post mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.07,
          "end": 62.1,
          "en": "If I want to send a link to someone that allows them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 64.26,
          "en": "to immediately create a new post,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.26,
          "end": 66.48,
          "en": "I could try to copy this URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.48,
          "end": 68.4,
          "en": "but if I paste it in and hit enter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.4,
          "end": 70.28999999999999,
          "en": "I end up on the starting page again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.28999999999999,
          "end": 74.4,
          "en": "because this React app has no pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.4,
          "end": 76.53,
          "en": "And that should generally make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.53,
          "end": 78.09,
          "en": "because as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.09,
          "end": 81.45,
          "en": "we're building a single page application with React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.45,
          "end": 85.56,
          "en": "so we have only one page, only one HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.56,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "But the idea behind routing is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 91.47,
          "en": "that we can still support multiple paths by simply listening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.47,
          "end": 95.22,
          "en": "to URL changes whilst the app is running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.22,
          "end": 99.03,
          "en": "or by evaluating the URL when it's first loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.03,
          "end": 102.9,
          "en": "and by then loading different components for different paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.9,
          "end": 105.57,
          "en": "that are encoded in the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.57,
          "end": 109.62,
          "en": "So that for our domain/nothing, we load the landing page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.62,
          "end": 113.43,
          "en": "for /products, we load the products page, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.43,
          "end": 114.783,
          "en": "That's routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.68,
          "end": 119.49000000000001,
          "en": "And even though React apps are SPAs, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.49000000000001,
          "end": 122.25,
          "en": "there is a solution for still getting this behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "And that's the React router package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 128.61,
          "en": "which is the most popular routing package for React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.61,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "because React itself has no routing capabilities built in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 134.88,
          "en": "And whilst you could build your own solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.88,
          "end": 139.26,
          "en": "where you try to take a look at the URL, extract the path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.26,
          "end": 142.05,
          "en": "and load different components for different paths,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.05,
          "end": 144.24,
          "en": "React Router is a powerful package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.24,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "that solves all these problems for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 150.24,
          "en": "and it offers tons of features related to routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.24,
          "end": 152.67000000000002,
          "en": "Now, just as with all the other React parts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.67000000000002,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "I dive way deeper into React Router in my full course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 159.87,
          "en": "but we'll still get started with this super useful package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.87,
          "end": 161.76,
          "en": "in this crash course here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.76,
          "end": 165.57,
          "en": "Now, React Router also has an official website where you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.57,
          "end": 167.85,
          "en": "of course, can also learn all about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.85,
          "end": 169.74,
          "en": "And it's also worth mentioning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.74,
          "end": 172.02,
          "en": "that there are different versions of this package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.02,
          "end": 175.2,
          "en": "And for example, version five is still quite popular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.2,
          "end": 177.9,
          "en": "but version six, for example, works quite differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.9,
          "end": 180.39,
          "en": "compared to version five, and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.39,
          "end": 183.84,
          "en": "I also got separate videos where I explain what's new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.84,
          "end": 186.66,
          "en": "in version six and also in 6.4 which also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.66,
          "end": 189.54,
          "en": "added even more exciting features to React Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.54,
          "end": 192.33,
          "en": "In this crash course, we're of course going to dive into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.33,
          "end": 193.803,
          "en": "that latest version here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.06,
          "end": 196.92000000000002,
          "en": "And for that, we first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.92000000000002,
          "end": 198.96,
          "en": "have to quit our development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.96,
          "end": 201,
          "en": "here in the front-end application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201,
          "end": 205.35,
          "en": "and run npm install react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 208.41,
          "en": "So not just react-router, but react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 208.41,
          "end": 209.88,
          "en": "This package must be installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.88,
          "end": 211.707,
          "en": "and that gives us React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.707,
          "end": 214.98,
          "en": "in this front-end application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.98,
          "end": 216.72,
          "en": "Now with that, we can add routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 216.72,
          "end": 219.39,
          "en": "and what's really important to keep in mind is that we still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.39,
          "end": 221.19,
          "en": "have a front-end application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.19,
          "end": 223.71,
          "en": "This routing happens on the client side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 223.71,
          "end": 228,
          "en": "not on some backend, but it does still enable us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 228,
          "end": 229.74,
          "en": "to support different paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.74,
          "end": 231.78,
          "en": "and simply load different components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.78,
          "end": 233.553,
          "en": "for those different paths.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
